tent":"off"},"207":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-205","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#workspace-workspace","content":"true or { dir?, persist? } — surface scratch files as result.artifacts + artifact:produced events"},"208":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-206","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#workspace-workspace","content":"Paths scratch/... or @scratch/... use the session scratch dir. Other paths use the project root. When project: false, unprefixed paths resolve to scratch. Scratch is cleaned up on session.close()."},"209":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-207","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#workspace-workspace","content":"When artifacts is enabled, files the agent writes to scratch are returned in result.artifacts ({ id, path, mime, bytes }) and emitted as artifact:produced events. With persist (default on for object form) they are copied under .agentkit/artifacts/<sessionId>/ so they survive scratch cleanup, and @agentkit/server serves them at GET /artifacts/:sessionId/:id. See SECURITY.md for the isolation model."},"210":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-208","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#built-in-tools-builtins","content":"Opt-in groups. Prefer workspace for filesystem/shell. builtins.groups.filesystem|shell is shimmed to workspace (deprecation warning once)."},"211":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-209","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#built-in-tools-builtins","content":"Group"},"212":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-210","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#built-in-tools-builtins","content":"Tools"},"213":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-211","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#built-in-tools