ing-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#install","content":"To try the SDK from a local clone before publish, see Local install & linking (git #path:, pnpm link, or file:)."},"418":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#building-with-an-ai-coding-agent","content":"AgentKit ships a single-file guide written for AI coding assistants: every feature, the full config, events, the server/client/hook APIs and recipes. Install it into your project and your assistant builds with the SDK instead of hand-rolling servers, reconnects or approval queues:"},"419":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#building-with-an-ai-coding-agent","content":"The same guide is LLM_GUIDE.md in the repo."},"420":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#minimal-agent","content":"Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY, or pass provider: { default: \"claude-...\", apiKey: \"...\" }. For local inference, use the built-in Ollama provider — see Providers and Models & switching."},"421":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#presets","content":"For UI, CLI, or backend jobs, start from a preset instead of an empty config:"},"422":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#presets","content":"See Configuration reference for createCLIPreset and createBackendPreset."},"423":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#browser-ui","content":"Run the agent on the server, connect from the browser:"},"424":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#browser-ui","content":"See Streaming & wire protocol for connect(), SSE events, and vanilla JS."},"425":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#example","content":"See examples/node-backend. Run with mock provider:"},"426":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"427":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"AgentKit headless agent runtime"},"428":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#install","content":"Install"},"429":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"Two levels"},"430":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"431":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"AgentKit is a TypeScript agent runtime you import into existing projects. The engine runs on Node; any UI connects over the AG-UI wire."},"432":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"From this monorepo:"},"433":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"createAgent(config) is the one-call path, and it covers most projects. Underneath it is a plugin kernel, and the same import gives you that too — services you can replace, extension points you can intercept, and a composition you can publish. That is what you reach for when you are building a coding agent or a domain harness rather than calling a model."},"434":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"See Extending AgentKit."},"435":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Getting started"},"436":{"id":"/