in write / delete / send categories (or names containing those strings) default to approve."},"689":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals-8","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/approvals#config","content":"Policies: \"auto\" (run immediately), \"approve\" (wait for human), \"deny\" (block)."},"690":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals-9","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/approvals#config","content":"autoApproveAfterMs approves a request on its own when nobody has decided it in time, through session.approve/reject or the admin plane, and reports it as by: \"timeout\" on approval:resolved. A demo that waits for a person but must not hang uses it; a programmatic onApproval decides alone and is not timed."},"691":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals-10","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/approvals#wire--react-ui","content":"Every settled approval emits approval:resolved ({ requestId, decision: \"approved\" | \"rejected\", by? }, by is session, telemetry, onApproval or none), whoever settled it, so every open UI can clear its prompt. Questions emit elicitation:resolved ({ requestId, answered }). session.stop() rejects the pending approvals of the run in flight and keeps the session."},"692":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals-11","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/approvals#approval-broker-for-custom-harnesses","content":"Outside createAgent (a @agentkit/runtime harness, a dashboard), createApprovalBroker({ autoApproveAfterMs? }) from @agentkit/runtime parks requests until a person decides:"},"693":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals-12","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/approvals#approval-broker-for-custom-harnesses","content":"examples/express-api registers gated_write with policies: { gated_write