building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#related","content":"Related"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-7","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","content":"Scope. What AgentKit gives you for a Claude Code or Codex-style product, what it deliberately leaves to you, and what is still missing. Not an IDE: you bring the terminal, web or desktop shell, AgentKit stays the headless engine.Audience. Teams building on @agentkit/core. Verified against the code on main, September 2026."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-8","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."},"1076":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-9","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"AgentKit is built for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"},"1077":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-10","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"examples/mini-harness: 