","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"GET /mcp, GET /mcp/:id/tools, POST /mcp/*"},"1943":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"rag.sources() / .ingest(docs) / .query(q, k?)"},"1944":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"/rag/* (ingest posts { docs })"},"1945":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"models.list() / .setDefault(id) / .test(id) / .add(cfg) / .refresh() / .remove(id) / .usage()"},"1946":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"/models/*"},"1947":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"Every call checks the response and throws AgentKitError { status, message, body } on failure."},"1948":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"createSessionHub(url, options?) does that routing for you: one /events/all stream, every event folded into its session's state with the reducers below, so sessions in the background keep updating while the UI shows another."},"1949":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Member"},"1950":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"session(id)"},"1951":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"A ClientSession for id (the same object per id): every call carries id, on / onAny see that session's events plus agent-wide ones (MCP, models) from the shared stream, send / answer emit client:send / client:answer, workflows.run closes the run in the hub's state when it returns. Pass it to any store or hook. Its close() detaches its listeners only"},"1952":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"state(id)"},"1953":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"{ conversation, pending, workflow, plan, todos, usage }; emptySessionState for a session it hasn't seen"},"1954":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"sessions() / subscribe(fn)"},"1955":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Ids it knows (from events, session(), seed(), create()), in order; fn runs after any change"},"1956":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"seed(id) / create() / forget(id)"},"1957":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Load history; start a session; drop one's state"},"1958":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"status / onStatus(fn) / close()"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"The shared stream"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-55","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"options are connect()'s (token, tenant, reconnect) plus conversation (passed to reduceConversation, e.g. { includeNested: true }). The hub loads the saved workflows (GET /workflows) on each (re)connect so a run shows every step up front."},"1961":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-56","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Pure reducers turn the event stream into the state a UI renders. They are (state, event) => state, so they work in any framework, in tests and in a plain <script type=\"module\">."},"1962":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-57","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Reducer"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-58","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"State"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-59","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceConversation"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-60","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ messages: [{ id, role, text, thinking?, tools, artifacts, parts, status, error? }], streaming } (status: streaming / done / stopped / error; stopped when the run was stopped, from done with status: \"stopped\") — parts interleave text, thinking, tool calls and questions (with the user's answer, from the local client:answer event); workflow-step and subagent events (scope) are left out unless { includeNested: true }"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-61","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reducePending"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-62","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ approvals, questions } — cleared by approval:resolved / elicitation:resolved, the gated tool's result, and run end"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-63","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceWorkflowRun"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-64","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ runs: [{ ru