y. sessionState(hub, sessionId) is a readable store of that session's { conversation, pending, workflow, plan, todos, usage }, and hubSessions(hub) of the ids it knows. hub.session(id) is a ClientSession the stores above accept. See Client."],[714,"Create or overwrite (approval by default)"],[2100,"Create or resume a wire session → { sessionId }"],[842,"Create the app at GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps. Its callback URL is where the sign-in lands:"],[1381,"create_subagent takes a name, a self-contained task, and (when a model set\nis configured) which model to use. The child gets a fixed identity, the\nparent's tools, none of the parent's conversation, and returns only its final\nanswer. Delegation is one level deep unless allowNesting is set. Several\ncreate_subagent calls in one step run concurrently when the parent was\ncreated with parallelToolCalls: true."],[2,"createAgent config, events, and wire API"],[1517,"createAgent is the one-call path: configuration goes in, an agent comes out. It covers the common case, and most projects never need anything else."],[577,"createAgent({ provider: \"anthropic\" })"],[5,"createAgent(config)"],[433,"createAgent(config) is the one-call path, and it covers most projects. Underneath it is a plugin kernel, and the same import gives you that too — services you can replace, extension points you can intercept, and a composition you can publish. That is what you reach for when you are building a coding agent or a domain harness rather than calling a model."],[378,"createAgent(config) returns an object with run, session, on, mcp, models, workflow, and related helpers. Configuration is validated at construction time with Zod."],[41,"createBackendPreset"],[568,"createBackendPreset"],[36,"createCLIPreset"],[564,"createCLIPreset"],[2354,"createGraphPlugin wires Plugin.onWorkflowGraph and onWorkflowNodeStatus for renderers (React Flow, Mermaid, logs):"],[626,"createHandoffTeam — triage → specialists via handoffs"],[29